# Physical sensor profile for the currently used X500; not a complete factory
# parameter dump, calibration backup, aircraft identity or arming permission.
# Each future drone gets its own file. Apply before mode and mission files.
# These are upstream Copter 4.7 parameters using METRES; older *_CM/GNDCLEAR
# names use other units. Unknown parameters must fail REAL upload before writes.
# Preserve the already installed hardware RNGFND1_TYPE: its model/interface has
# not been specified. The REAL uploader rejects disabled/SITL sensor backends
# when applying this profile. A parameter readback is not sensor health proof.
# Metadata (pinned firmware):
# https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/dbe792162d06cab66c3475fd5556bf7a120f119e/libraries/AP_RangeFinder/AP_RangeFinder_Params.cpp

# RNGFND1_ORIENT -- mounting-direction enum: 25 = down, 24 = up, 0 = forward.
# The installed sensor faces down for landing height. This declares the sensor
# orientation; it does not rotate UAV yaw, move hardware or guarantee good data.
# SITL sets its physical simulated beam separately using SIM_SONAR_ROT=25.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#rngfnd1-orient
RNGFND1_ORIENT 25

# RNGFND1_MIN -- minimum reliable range, metres. User sensor limit: 0.15 = 15 cm.
# Readings below this are OutOfRangeLow, not healthy zero-height readings. REAL
# retains this actual dead zone; SITL mode deliberately overrides it to zero
# for idealized native height/retry tests without changing this physical profile.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#rngfnd1-min
RNGFND1_MIN 0.15

# RNGFND1_MAX -- maximum reliable range, metres. User sensor limit: 12 m.
# Greater ranges are OutOfRangeHigh; a 15 m RTL return may lack usable height
# until descending. This limit does not extend target-camera detection range,
# select RTL destination, relax GPS checks or authorize blind touchdown.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#rngfnd1-max
RNGFND1_MAX 12

# RNGFND1_GNDCLR -- expected grounded sensor-to-surface range, metres.
# Official metadata: "This parameter sets the expected range measurement that
# the range finder should return when the vehicle is on the ground".
# User measurement: 0.17 = 17 cm, only 2 cm above the 15 cm minimum. Validate
# mounting/noise near contact. This is GNDCLR, not GNCLR or legacy centimetre
# GNDCLEAR. EKF assumptions use it; it does not clamp frontend readings, place
# the sensor, cure unhealthy data, set deck/Home altitude or detect touchdown.
# SITL mode deliberately overrides it to zero; never use that override on REAL.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#rngfnd1-gndclr
RNGFND1_GNDCLR 0.17
